# DRIVE Product Rules

- Before coding, read every file in `docs/`, especially `00-product-brief.md`, `01-mvp-scope.md`, and `02-game-design-rules.md`.
- DRIVE rewards execution quality, not just completion. Protect pacing discipline, rate control, consistency, honest uploads, reflection, improvement, good habits, and coach verified effort.
- Keep the MVP centred on coach-created quests, PM5 photo upload, athlete reflection, coach verification, rewards, squad missions, River Map, and Boathouse progress.
- Do not add unrequested features. Future possibilities are not permission to build OCR, Concept2 API, live PM5 Bluetooth, Unity, Godot, social features, or pure speed leaderboards.
- Do not turn DRIVE into a generic workout tracker or metres leaderboard.
- Do not change unrelated files. Keep each task scoped to the user's request.
- If a request conflicts with the docs, stop and explain the conflict before implementing.
- After every task, summarise changed files and explain how each change supports the DRIVE brief.
